      "memo_sha256": "acb4b060c82f693425eb1f2e51c469fa40ba48cb33690b7fb4b6794f097846e5",
      "report_home": 4,
      "source_reading": "The Nash proposition says that no applicant benefits ex ante from deviating from the top-k set, but it does not define the payoff functional, feasible-deviation domain, or success-law coupling needed to state that claim as a finite mathematical theorem."
    },
